<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>Mountaineers Cruise Past Georgia Southern in Sun Belt Quarterfinals</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/mens-soccer-mountaineers-cruise-past-georgia-southern-in-sun-belt-quarterfinals</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/mens-soccer-mountaineers-cruise-past-georgia-southern-in-sun-belt-quarterfinals</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Men's Soccer celebrates after scoring a goal" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MSOC_vsGeorgiaSouthern_Nov8_2026_AM-45.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 9 West Virginia University men's soccer team rolled to a 4-0 victory over Georgia Southern in the Sun Belt quarterfinals, Sunday afternoon at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium. The top-seeded Mountaineers improve to 11-2-4 overall and advance to the semifinals against the winner between James Madison and Coastal Carolina.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MSOC_vsGeorgiaSouthern_Nov8_2026_AM-45.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MSOC_vsGeorgiaSouthern_Nov8_2026_AM-45.jpg"><media:title>Men's Soccer celebrates after scoring a goal</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/9/MSOC_vsGeorgiaSouthern_Nov8_2026_AM-45.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:44:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59666</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Capture Second Ranked Win of the Season for Second Time in Program History</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/volleyball-mountaineers-capture-second-ranked-win-of-the-season-for-second-time-in-program-history</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/volleyball-mountaineers-capture-second-ranked-win-of-the-season-for-second-time-in-program-history</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball sings Country Roads following a 3-1 victory over No. 25 Colorado" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/8/VB_WVUvsColorado_11-8_ECCOUNTRYRDS-2.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (12-10, 5-7 Big 12) matched its single-season program record for ranked wins with a four-set victory over No. 25 Colorado on Sunday afternoon at Hope Coliseum, taking down the Buffaloes, 3-1, by set scores of 25-23, 23-25, 25-17 and 25-11.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/VB_WVUvsColorado_11-8_ECCOUNTRYRDS-2.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/VB_WVUvsColorado_11-8_ECCOUNTRYRDS-2.jpg"><media:title>WVU Volleyball sings Country Roads following a 3-1 victory over No. 25 Colorado</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/VB_WVUvsColorado_11-8_ECCOUNTRYRDS-2.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:49:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59665</s:story_id></item><item><title>No. 8-Seed WVU Set to Begin Play at 2026 Big 12 Tournament</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-soccer-no-8-seed-wvu-set-to-begin-play-at-2026-big-12-tournament</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-soccer-no-8-seed-wvu-set-to-begin-play-at-2026-big-12-tournament</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="The WVU women's soccer team poses for a group photo at Texas Health Mansfield Stadium before the 2026 Big 12 Tournament." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Big_12_Tournament-20.jpg" /><br /><br />MANSFIELD, Texas – The West Virginia University women's soccer team opens postseason play at the 2026 Big 12 Soccer Tournament on Monday, Nov. 9, in Mansfield, Texas. The No. 8-seeded Mountaineers will take on No. 1-seed BYU at 3 p.m. ET/2 p.m. CT inside Texas Health Mansfield Stadium.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Big_12_Tournament-20.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Big_12_Tournament-20.jpg"><media:title>The WVU women's soccer team poses for a group photo at Texas Health Mansfield Stadium before the 2026 Big 12 Tournament.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Big_12_Tournament-20.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:27:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59664</s:story_id></item><item><title>WVU Rolls Past Georgia Tech on the Road</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-basketball-wvu-rolls-past-georgia-tech-on-the-road</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-basketball-wvu-rolls-past-georgia-tech-on-the-road</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Marya Hudgins celebrates the Mountaineers win over Georgia Tech" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/8/THIRD_QUARTER_DW-18.jpg" /><br /><br />ATLANTA, Ga. – The No. 24 West Virginia women's basketball team improved to 3-0 on the season with an 81-63 road victory over Georgia Tech on Sunday afternoon at McCamish Pavilion.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/THIRD_QUARTER_DW-18.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/THIRD_QUARTER_DW-18.jpg"><media:title>Marya Hudgins celebrates the Mountaineers win over Georgia Tech</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/8/THIRD_QUARTER_DW-18.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:23:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>9</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59663</s:story_id></item><item><title>Ingleton, Nickel Highlight 2026 All-Big 12 Team Honors</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-soccer-ingleton-nickel-highlight-2026-all-big-12-team-honors</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/8/womens-soccer-ingleton-nickel-highlight-2026-all-big-12-team-honors</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Nyema Ingleton and Sophia Nickel compete during home matches at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/8/Ny__Soph_2-up.png" /><br /><br />MANSFIELD, Texas – Four members of the West Virginia University women's soccer team have been named to the 2026 All-Big 12 Teams, the league announced on Sunday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusp